export anchor TestDiscovery:
    description:
        The project is the piton.config.pi in the working directory. Every .pi
        file under its source root is compiled, not only what the entry reaches,
        and every concrete anchor declared with export that has @piton/test's
        Test in its inheritance chain is a test, wherever in the source root it
        is, and whatever keyword or chain it got there by. Tests in tethers/
        belong to installed packages and are left out. The plugin finds them
        with one query of the compiled project, described in the plugin API.
        Tests are ordered by the file they are declared in, then by name, so a
        run and a listing order them the same way every time.

        The project has to compile cleanly first: tests are not run over a
        specification with errors, which are reported as diagnostics and stop
        the run. So does a test that isn't well-formed, one whose expects is
        empty or whose against isn't spec, code or both: each is reported by
        name with the file it is in, and none of the tests run.
